  "prompt": "Which expression is equivalent to $3x(2x^{2}-5x+4)-x(x^{2}+2x-3)$?",
  "choices": {
    "A": "$5x^{3}-17x^{2}+9x$",
    "B": "$5x^{3}-13x^{2}+15x$",
    "C": "$5x^{3}-17x^{2}+15x$",
    "D": "$7x^{3}-17x^{2}+15x$"
  },
  "correctAnswer": "C",
  "explanation": "Distribute $3x$ into the first parentheses: $3x(2x^2-5x+4) = 6x^3-15x^2+12x$. Distribute $x$ into the second parentheses: $x(x^2+2x-3) = x^3+2x^2-3x$. Subtract the second from the first: $(6x^3-15x^2+12x)-(x^3+2x^2-3x) = 6x^3-x^3-15x^2-2x^2+12x+3x = 5x^3-17x^2+15x$.",
